<h2>Where the DIR sits in the scheme</h2>
<p>Section 2(e) of the DV Act defines a domestic incident report as a report made in the prescribed form on receipt of a complaint of domestic violence from an aggrieved person. Three provisions give it work to do: Section 9(1)(b) makes it the Protection Officer's duty to prepare the DIR and forward it to the Magistrate and the police; Section 10(2)(a) empowers a service provider to record the DIR; and the proviso to Section 12(1) directs that before passing any order on an application, the Magistrate shall take into consideration any DIR received from the Protection Officer or service provider.</p>
<table class="law">
